  "reading": "The two fixed-size nulls answer a power question at one effect size: could this design have seen a shared order separated as widely as the pooled estimates? It could. The own-gap nulls impose only the order at the separations actually estimated: every target keeps its own level and its own gap magnitudes, including targets whose middle two qualities sit a few steps apart. own_gaps_deconvolved is the honest version of that, because observed within-target spread is inflated by measurement noise. What no simulation at an estimated separation can exclude is a shared order separated by much less than that; the gap-scale sweep bounds those worlds instead, and within these families shared orders separated by at least smallest_excluded_separation_steps are excluded. Two limits apply to all of it: the ordered truths are plug-in constructions from the observed estimates, not a profile over every per-target truth compatible with a common order, and each target's four qualities are perturbed independently at their marginal standard errors while the source bootstrap resamples the four together. These are therefore conditional sensitivity results, not an exclusion of the composite hypothesis in general.",
